{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551409-examples-of-heroes-used-in-other-media","id":551409,"title":"Examples of Heroes used in other media","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-12T07:31:59-07:00","id":551409,"title":"Examples of Heroes used in other media","content":"So after re reading the kickstarter I thought of three character that fit the criteria stated in heroes section such as they are obsessed to one character have an integrity of four or lower and is no longer<br /> <br /> Ulysses S Grant (Fallout New Vegas)<br /> <br /> This guy hates the Courier(PC), He hates him so much that he hunted him down everywhere. Why does he hate the Courier well the reason for this apparently the Courier was hired to bring a package back to his home as well so not only was he doing his job but was also able to go back to his home. Problem is the package activated dozens of warheads right under his community destroying not only his home but turning his community into the most dangerous place on earth. Ulysses comes into place here because he retired in the Couriers community after years for working for Caesar and not only does he witnesses the explosion but was caught in it as well. He survives and goes out to hunt the Courier for what he did. Problem is the Courier has no idea that he destroyed his community and Ulysses proceeds to cause more damage then the Courier in fact nearly every DLC story you do was caused by him Honest Hearts he teaches a tribe how to use firearms and how to destroy communities<br /> in his hunt for the Courier he told a clearly homicidal man how to get a very powerful weapon in hopes of killing him and to top it off he broke a logic loop of the think thank a group of very powerful scientists who have survived the war and lost their ethics and moral and by Ulysses words were the &quot;gods of the old world&quot; and they can do way more damage than what the nuclear war . Ulysses is obsessed with finding a deeper meaning in nearly anything the Courier does because to him the Divide was not an accident to him the Courier mythologized for what he did to the point where he treats the actual title not as a person but an unstoppable force of nature whose message is their ability to destroy entire worlds and leave chaos in their wake. The problem with Ulysses is unlike the Courier who did this with no intent of harm Ulysses does damage with intent.<br /> <br /> Handsome jack (borderlands)<br /> <br /> This guy considers himself a hero no matter what he does destroy a town full of civilians &quot;they were bandits&quot; kill a group of scientists &quot;they were going to back stab you so you should probably thank me&quot; <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">He has no real understanding of the concept of &quot;good&quot;. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">He is so convinced that he's the hero that he will occasionally do stupid things because he thinks its being heroic</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> such as when he tortures Tannis but lets her live, thinking he's being &quot;merciful.&quot; </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">His twisted understanding of the concept of &quot;good&quot;. In his eyes, a hero is something you can just say you are and enforce using the right words. (&quot;Because that's what heroes do. We're merciful.&quot; &quot;You don't do things because they're easy, you do them because they're right!&quot;) in his mind he is the hero of this story regardless of whatever he does from killing his employees to using his own daughter as a battery. all his enemies are bandits and everyone loves him just hear this quote </span></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>&quot;<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hey kids, do you know what your mommies and daddies gave up to live here in Opportunity? Literally nothing! </span></i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">You're paid to be here!</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i> I'm the one who feeds and protects everyone. Remember , we should all love our parents, but love me more<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Narcissist\" target=\"_blank\">.&quot;</a></i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Jason Brody (Farcry 3)<br /> <br /> The Protagonist of the game he and his friends get captured by vaas Jason escapes see his brother die and just wants to save his friends and leave the island to safety and he does this in the beginning saves his friends check found a way out check but the problem is Jason is having so much fun in the island killing people, animals and the adrenaline that comes with this and decides instead of getting him and his friends out like he promised he opts to go out and destroy vaas empire just for fun and revenge oh he also cheats on his girlfriend with vaas sister. He changed from this college student who was afraid of seeing people die regardless if they are a pirate or not into a guy who has fun from hunting anything humans and animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},