sts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:45:01-07:00","id":551586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551409-examples-of-heroes-used-in-other-media?p=551481#post551481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpicking, but that description of Brody is kind of inaccurate for his character arc and assumes the player took one of the two possible endings instead of considering both. And the ending you pick has immense significance to any interpretation you make of his development.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken I was thinking about the part where brody takes some strong drugs and vaas sister decided to have fun with his body while knocked out<br /> <br /> I agree with punisher seeing that he also targets children without knowing if they were good or bad(runaways)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:59:57-07:00","id":551616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551409-examples-of-heroes-used-in-other-media?p=551575#post551575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Punisher count as a Hero?<br /> Family killed by mobsters, psyche hurt, becomes someone who hunts down and murders criminals, including some seriously trivial ones.<br /> <br /> Coming to think about it, Yagami Light from Death Note would both count as a Beast and Hero. Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Version of the Punisher, one of them fits abit better backstory wise, He had a mild case of PTSD and was going too retire anyway, Retired and then had his family caught in the crossfire of the Mafia and the Yakuza, Considers all Criminal and Crimes too be worth Death (If they have hurt innocents anyway).<br /> <br /> Arcturus Mengsk from Starcraft, He's willing to let an entire Planet and it's people get wiped out just too get support to go after his Target, he is obstensively doing it too &quot;Save&quot; his people from the UED. Generally an Arse.<br /> <br /> Heero Yuy, from Gundam Wing, Someone who has been raised as an assassin, explicitly finds it hard too identify with normal people, only comes into his own while in combat. Or after he's had a chance too see things from another perspective, he's still not a normal &quot;Person&quot; by the end, but he's atleast capable of understanding he doesn't HAVE too be a weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:08:13-07:00","id":551647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/551409-examples-of-heroes-used-in-other-media?p=551616#post551616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arcturus Mengsk from Starcraft, He's willing to let an entire Planet and it's people get wiped out just too get support to go after his Target, he is obstensively doing it too &quot;Save&quot; his people from the UED. Generally an Arse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I would label Mengsk as something like an Invictus Ventrue or a Seer, this is an interesting angle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:34:37-07:00","id":551706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_pos